# Team conventions — who answers from where

Clone-owned prose slot. The triage skill reads this before deciding that a
customer mail is unanswered, because every automated check it has looks at
**{{ accounts_default }}@'s own Sent archive** — and a teammate replying from a
mailbox that never touches {{ accounts_default }}@ is invisible to all of them.

Fill in, for this company:

- **Who replies to customers, and from which address.** Name the mailboxes that
  handle customer mail without going through {{ email_address }}.
- **When a thread is deliberately left to a human**, and how you can tell —
  a label, an assignment, a phrase people use.
- **Which senders are internal or automated**, so they are never treated as a
  customer waiting for an answer.
- **Anything the Sent archive cannot see**: replies by phone, in a portal, via a
  shared inbox, or forwarded out to somebody else to handle.

If this file is empty, the operator has to assume {{ accounts_default }}@'s Sent
archive is the whole story. Where that is not true, it will draft a reply to
somebody a colleague has already answered — so write down what it cannot see.
